# Deployment

| Branch / event       | Target                              |
| -------------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| Push to `master`     | prod (`climbing-timer-3f18c`)       |
| Push to `beta`       | beta site                           |
| Pull request         | Firebase preview channel (30 days)  |

All deploys run:

```bash
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile && pnpm build && firebase deploy
```

CI config lives in `.github/workflows/`. When changing deploy flow, update
**both** the relevant workflow file *and* `firebase.json` targets — they must
stay in sync or deploys will land in the wrong project.

`pnpm build` includes `tsc` and **`pnpm lint` fails on any warning**, so
preview deploys will fail if lint is dirty. Fix lint locally before pushing.
